+# Branch Architecture
+
+Status: consolidation is complete **locally**. Nothing has been pushed. Verification is static only; no full kernel build or CI run has been performed.
+
+## Long-lived refs
+
+| Ref | Purpose |
+|---|---|
+| `common/base` | Single development base. Derived from `onyx`, with the dangling `drivers/kernelsu` symlink removed. Code-base tag: `base-v1`. The later documentation commit on `common/base` is metadata only; feature branches were cut from `base-v1`. |
+| `feature/ksun` | KernelSU-Next + SUSFS + NoMount. |
+| `feature/bakasu` | Bakasu root + SUSFS + NoMount. |
+| `feature/resukisu` | ReSukiSU root + SUSFS + NoMount. |
+| `feature/apatch` | APatch/FolkPatch build wiring + NoMount. |
+| `feature/miui` | MIUI/HyperOS WLAN compatibility. |
+| `feature/c2` | MT6785 vcodec/VCU and C2 media stack. |
+| `release/*` | Immutable release tags. No long-lived integration branches. |
+| `archive/*` | Snapshots of superseded or source branches, retained before any branch deletion. |
+
+## Base invariants
+
+`common/base` keeps the `onyx` performance work:
+
+- WALT and the tuned PELT half-life.
+- ARMv8 crypto extensions and hardware acceleration.
+- BFQ with the onyx tuning, zram writeback, and zstd.
+- xswapd and gaming-mode/dynamic-fsync behavior.
+- TRB Clang 18 via `kerdevdep/setup_kerdevdep.sh`.
+
+Feature branches must not remove those settings. Several imported root branches originally carried older `begonia_user_defconfig` states that disabled WALT or crypto; those regressions were reverted so the feature branches keep the base configuration.
+
+## Features
+
+| Branch | Source | Scope | Notes |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| `feature/ksun` | `onyx-ksu-next` | `KernelSU` gitlink, `drivers/kernelsu` symlink, SUSFS, NoMount, KSU patches | `build.sh` recognizes `feature/ksun`; recursive submodules are required. |
+| `feature/bakasu` | `onyx-bakasu` | In-tree `drivers/kernelsu`, SUSFS, NoMount | Bakasu defconfig keeps WALT/crypto/BFQ/zram. |
+| `feature/resukisu` | `onyx-resukisu` | In-tree `drivers/kernelsu`, SUSFS, NoMount | Uses `resukisu_defconfig`. |
+| `feature/apatch` | `onyx-apatch` | APatch/FolkPatch build wiring, NoMount | No KernelSU/SUSFS stack. |
+| `feature/miui` | `onyx-miui` | MIUI/HyperOS WLAN compatibility | Five-file scope: WLAN driver/adaptor, `net/wireless/core.c`, workflow, build script. |
+| `feature/c2` | `onyx-c2-ksun` | MT6785 vcodec/VCU, C2 media, cpufreq and PMIC changes | C2-only. No root, NoMount, SUSFS, or MIUI files. |
+
+SUSFS and NoMount are deliberately bundled with the root feature that consumes them. They are not separate features. Sultan/APatch build flavor wiring is likewise part of the APatch feature rather than a separate branch.
+
+## What was intentionally not made a feature
+
+- `feature/perf` was not created. `onyx` already contains the WALT, crypto, BFQ, zram writeback/zstd, xswapd, and gaming work. The apparent BFQ/zram changes in `main`/`granite`/`obsidian` are older states that would revert onyx tuning (for example BFQ slice-idle values and zram defaults), not additive improvements.
+- `main`, `granite`, `obsidian`, `hos3-fix`, and `onyx-kaeru` are treated as superseded/archive sources. `onyx-kaeru` has been retained as requested. Their heads are preserved as `archive/<name>` tags.
+- C2 Saikrishna commits are included only in C2 content. The recent C2 cherry-picks were empty or redundant against the local C2 media stack, so no Saikrishna-only changes were added to non-C2 features.
+
+## Release tags
+
+| Tag | Defconfig | Contents |
+|---|---|---|
+| `release/onyx-ksu-next-2026-10-20` | `begonia_ksu_next_defconfig` | KernelSU-Next + SUSFS + NoMount |
+| `release/onyx-c2-ksu-next-2026-10-20` | `begonia_ksu_next_defconfig` | C2 + KernelSU-Next + SUSFS + NoMount |
+| `release/onyx-miui-ksu-next-2026-10-20` | `begonia_ksu_next_defconfig` | MIUI/HyperOS + KernelSU-Next + SUSFS + NoMount |
+| `release/onyx-miui-bakasu-2026-10-20` | `bakasu_defconfig` | MIUI/HyperOS + Bakasu + SUSFS + NoMount |
+| `release/onyx-c2-bakasu-2026-10-20` | `bakasu_defconfig` | C2 + Bakasu + SUSFS + NoMount |
+| `release/onyx-apatch-2026-10-20` | `begonia_apatch_defconfig` | APatch/FolkPatch + NoMount |
+
+A separate `aosp-ksun-susfs` tag is unnecessary because SUSFS is already inside `feature/ksun`.
+
+## Building
+
+`build.sh` chooses its variant from `GIT_BRANCH`. On a detached tag, pass the tag name explicitly:
+
+```sh
+GIT_BRANCH=$(git describe --tags --exact-match) bash build.sh
+```
+
+or:
+
+```sh
+GIT_BRANCH=release/onyx-ksu-next-2026-10-20 bash build.sh
+GIT_BRANCH=release/onyx-miui-bakasu-2026-10-20 bash build.sh
+```
+
+For feature work:
+
+```sh
+GIT_BRANCH=feature/ksun bash build.sh
+GIT_BRANCH=feature/c2 bash build.sh
+```
+
+`build.sh` recognizes the `feature/*` names and the `release/<edition>-<date>` tags directly, including combined editions such as `release/onyx-c2-ksu-next-*`. `DEFCONFIG`, `VERSION_NAME`, `PACKAGE_NAME`, and `EXTRA_FLAGS` can be overridden explicitly if the branch/tag name is not part of the normal matrix. If the branch asks for a feature defconfig that is absent from the current checkout, `build.sh` warns and falls back to `begonia_user_defconfig` instead of failing in kconfig.
+
+### Build metadata and mirrors
+
+Every packaged build writes `build/build-info.env` and `build/build-info.json`
+(edition, branch, commit, defconfig, sizes, sha256/md5). CI sources this file
+instead of re-deriving artifact identity from the branch name.
+
+```sh
+./build.sh info          # print the metadata for the latest artifact
+./build.sh gofile        # mirror to Gofile   (GOFILE_TOKEN / GOFILE_FOLDER_ID optional)
+./build.sh pixeldrain    # mirror to PixelDrain (PIXELDRAIN_API_KEY required)
+./build.sh upload        # best-effort mirror to every configured provider
+```
+
+Mirror results are written to `build/gofile.env` and `build/pixeldrain.env`.
+
+### Kernel identity
+
+`uname -r` shows the short, stable release `4.14.357-Pox`. The full
+edition-qualified identity (`4.14.357-Pox-<version>-<edition>`) is kept as the
+extended version and shown in the build log, the flashable `CHANGELOG.txt`, the
+installer banner, and `build-info.env` as `LOCALVERSION_EXTENDED`. The builder
+banner is `POX@poxproject`. The commit id is excluded from both version strings
+(`CONFIG_LOCALVERSION_AUTO` is disabled during configuration); it is still
+recorded in the build metadata, the changelog, and the `<commit>.zip` link.
+
+`LOCALVERSION` overrides the short string, and `EXTENDED_LOCALVERSION` overrides
+the extended one.
+
+## Verification and cleanup state
+
+Static checks passed on every release combination:
+
+- `bash -n build.sh`.
+- No conflict markers.
+- Base config keys retained: WALT, ARMv8 crypto, BFQ, zram, zram writeback, zstd.
+- Variant keys present: KernelSU/SUSFS/NoMount or APatch/NoMount as applicable.
+- Feature isolation checked by changed-file scope.
+- TRB Clang 18 bootstrap present.
+- `git diff --check` reports only pre-existing trailing whitespace in imported root/NoMount code (not conflict markers).
+- An upstream fetch on 2026-10-20 confirmed the upstream branch tips were unchanged since the audit; it added upstream release tags only.
+
+The six ephemeral `test/*` integration branches were deleted after their release tags were created. Old branches are still present locally and have `archive/*` tags; they have not been deleted pending final approval. No push has been done.
