+# Conflict Log
+
+Consolidation date: 2026-10-20. This file records migration and integration conflicts. A recorded resolution is intentional; it was not applied silently.
+
+## C2 Saikrishna cherry-picks
+
+The local C2 media stack already contained the relevant Saikrishna changes. The recent commits were therefore empty, redundant, or resolved in favor of the local PoX C2 logic. No Saikrishna-only change was copied into a non-C2 feature.
+
+| Commit | Subject | Result |
+|---|---|---|
+| `ef187181c` | `media: mtk-vcodec: Port VCU and V4L2 vcodec driver for Codec2` | Conflict in `drivers/media/platform/mtk-vcodec/mtk_vcodec_dec.c`. The local stack has an extra guard in `vb2ops_vdec_stop_streaming()`: `if (dst_buf->state != VB2_BUF_STATE_ACTIVE) continue;`. The guard was preserved. The resulting cherry-pick was empty and was skipped. |
+| `a17a72d86` | Same vcodec port, sibling commit | Empty against the local C2 stack; skipped. |
+| `92f1a67bd` | C2 cpufreq change | Empty against the local C2 stack; skipped. |
+| `03fe2ea85` | `media: mtk-vcodec: mt6785: Release MMQoS frequency request when idle` | Conflicts in `mtk_vcodec_dec_pm.c` and `mtk_vcodec_enc_pm.c`. The local PoX anti-lag DVFS logic already releases MMQoS when idle and additionally holds warm clocks during active playback. Local logic was kept; the incoming patch was redundant and the cherry-pick was skipped. |
+| `17057c3d7` | C2 PMIC change | Empty against the local C2 stack; skipped. |
+
+Sibling/duplicate commits `e50f4bc1d`, `87a5b2975`, and `8ef08bda1` were not applied separately. `e50f4bc1d` has the same patch ID as `17057c3d7`, and `87a5b2975` has the same patch ID as `92f1a67bd`; the remaining sibling was redundant with the already-present C2 content.
+
+The C2 content is nevertheless present in `feature/c2` and in the C2 release tags. The cherry-pick history is empty because the local C2 stack was already at or ahead of those patches.
+
+## Integration merges
+
+The following ephemeral combinations were merged with `git merge --no-ff`:
+
+- AOSP + KernelSU-Next
+- AOSP + APatch
+- C2 + KernelSU-Next
+- C2 + Bakasu
+- MIUI + KernelSU-Next
+- MIUI + Bakasu
+
+All six merges completed automatically. A later MIUI configuration cleanup was merged into the two MIUI combinations; it only restored base `begonia_user_defconfig` and `begonia_apatch_defconfig` values. No conflict markers remain in any release tag.
+
+## Configuration regressions corrected during migration
+
+The imported root branches were based on older `onyx` states and several carried defconfig changes that would have disabled base functionality. These were corrected before release tagging:
+
+- `feature/ksun`: restored base `begonia_user_defconfig` and the dynamic-fsync behavior in `gaming_mode.c`.
+- `feature/resukisu`: restored base `begonia_user_defconfig`.
+- `feature/apatch`: restored base `begonia_user_defconfig`.
+- `feature/miui`: restored base security/performance values in the user and APatch defconfigs; kept only the WLAN compatibility changes plus the MIUI version/build wiring.
+- `feature/ksun`: added a `feature/ksun` build-script alias so the branch selects `begonia_ksu_next_defconfig`; restored the executable mode of `build.sh`.
+
+## Whitespace and non-conflicts
+
+`git diff --check` reports trailing whitespace in imported SUSFS/NoMount/root code. These are pre-existing whitespace issues, not conflict markers. Warning-line counts observed on the integration tips were:
+
+- KernelSU-Next combinations: 56 lines.
+- Bakasu combinations: 240 lines.
+- APatch: 14 lines.
+
+No actual `<<<<<<< ` or `>>>>>>> ` markers were found. No full kernel build was run, so this log does not claim a compile or runtime result.
