+# Contributing
+
+This repository uses a small, tag-based integration model rather than long-lived integration branches.
+
+## Branch model
+
+- Start feature work from `common/base`.
+- Keep one feature per `feature/*` branch. Do not mix root, MIUI, and C2 changes in one feature branch.
+- Do not create permanent `dev`, `integration`, or `test` branches. Integration branches are ephemeral and must be replaced by `release/*` tags.
+- Never force-push `common/base`, `release/*`, or `archive/*`.
+- Archive the source head as `archive/<name>` before deleting any old branch.
+- Do not push a consolidation or release ref until the diff, configuration, and build story have been checked.
+
+## Feature rules
+
+1. Keep the base performance stack intact: WALT, ARMv8 crypto, BFQ tuning, zram writeback/zstd, xswapd, and gaming/dynamic-fsync behavior.
+2. Do not copy an older full-tree state over `common/base`. Apply the smallest path-limited change that provides the feature.
+3. Root features own their SUSFS/NoMount bundle. Do not split SUSFS or NoMount into separate features.
+4. APatch is its own root/build feature. Do not add KernelSU/SUSFS content to it.
+5. C2-only patches belong in `feature/c2`; do not add them to non-C2 features.
+6. MIUI/HyperOS compatibility is WLAN-focused. It must not weaken base security or performance configuration without an explicit, documented reason.
+7. If a feature needs a new build variant, update `build.sh` so the feature branch name itself selects the correct defconfig.
+
+## Integration and release
+
+Use an ephemeral branch only for validation:
+
+```sh
+git switch -c test/<combo> common/base
+git merge --no-ff feature/<name> -m "test: integrate <name>"
+```
+
+Resolve conflicts deliberately. Record every non-trivial resolution in `CONFLICTS.md`; do not silently choose one side. Then run the static checklist:
+
+```sh
+bash -n build.sh
+git grep -n -E '^(<<<<<<<|>>>>>>>) ' HEAD -- .
+git diff --check common/base..HEAD
+```
+
+`git diff --check` may report trailing whitespace in imported root/NoMount code. That is not a conflict, but it must be documented rather than hidden.
+
+Check the selected defconfig for the base keys and the feature keys:
+
+```sh
+git show HEAD:arch/arm64/configs/<defconfig> | grep -E 'CONFIG_(SCHED_WALT|CRYPTO_AES_ARM64|IOSCHED_BFQ|ZRAM|ZRAM_WRITEBACK|CRYPTO_ZSTD|KSU|KSU_SUSFS|NOMOUNT|KALLSYMS_ALL)='
+```
+
+When the combination passes, create an immutable annotated tag:
+
+```sh
+git tag -a release/<combo>-YYYY-MM-DD <commit> -m "Release <combo>"
+```
+
+Then delete the ephemeral `test/*` branch. Do not keep it as a long-lived branch.
+
+## Building
+
+`build.sh` derives the variant from `GIT_BRANCH`. For a detached tag, set it explicitly:
+
+```sh
+GIT_BRANCH=$(git describe --tags --exact-match) bash build.sh
+```
+
+If the branch name is outside the normal matrix:
+
+```sh
+GIT_BRANCH=feature/<name> DEFCONFIG=<defconfig> VERSION_NAME="<name>" bash build.sh
+```
+
+## Commit style
+
+Use a scoped subject such as:
+
+```text
+feat(ksun): import KernelSU-Next + SUSFS + NoMount stack
+fix(miui): keep base security and performance config
+build(ksun): recognize feature/ksun branch name
+```
+
+Explain source branches and intentional omissions in the body when a feature is squashed from an unrelated history. Do not claim a build or runtime test that was not performed.
+
+## Cleanup and archive policy
+
+- `common/base` and `feature/*` are the working refs.
+- `release/*` tags are immutable release snapshots.
+- `archive/<name>` tags preserve old branch heads.
+- Keep `onyx-kaeru` unless the maintainer explicitly approves its removal.
+- Delete old branches only after their archive tag exists, and only with maintainer approval.
